# Mock data

All hackathon data lives under `mock-data/`. Import with `@/mock-data/...`. Do not embed catalogs in components.

## Shape

**Universities** — `UNIVERSITIES` → university → **course category** (e.g. Computer Science) → **course** `{ name, code }` (e.g. Matrices and Determinants, `MTH 111`).

**General skills** — `SKILL_CATEGORIES` → category (Programming, Design, Photography, Life skill) → **skill** `{ name }` (Python, barbing, swimming).

**Users** — `BARTER_USERS` in `users.ts`: `{ username, name, email, bio, avatar/cover, skills, education, … }`. Listings reference `username`; the public page is `/users/<username>`.

## Rules

- Typed `interface`s in `mock-data/types.ts`
- One concern per file (`universities.ts`, `skills.ts`)
- Ids are stable slugs (`unn`, `unilag`)
- Extend catalogs here when Figma needs more rows; do not invent a backend
